<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 13,779 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 13,779 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 13,779 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Saturday compared to 44,820 tonnes in the same period on Friday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Saturday    August 1</p>
<p>    Export cargo		 6,066	 9,650</p>
<p>    Import cargo		 7,713	35,170</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, one ship sailed and two berthed. In the next 24 hours, four are expected to sail and 15 are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Fuel oil	     42,000	 Trade Resolve	   2/8</p>
<p>High speed diesel  70,000	 Chesapeak City	  4/8</p>
<p>Vegetable oil	18,600	 Kristal		   4/8</p>
<p>High speed diesel  34,500	 Al-Sabiyah		4/8</p>
<p>-- Karachi Newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
